      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First off, I'm not a doctor, but I can give you some advice. Ringworm, or tinea corporis, is a fungal infection, so antibiotics won't help. Ibuprofen is great for pain, but it won't kill the fungus. You should see a doctor, but if that's not an option, you can try a topical antifungal cream, like clotrimazole or terbinafine. Apply it to the affected area twice a day. Keep the area clean and dry. If it doesn't improve in a week, see a doctor. Remember, self-treatment can be risky, so use caution.",
      "source": "target",
